    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Squamous cell carcinoma of the right tonsillar pillar, p16-negative, suspected at presentation and confirmed by biopsy at the otolaryngology visit; linked to the documented 1885 diagnosis: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Nicotine dependence, cigars, about ten a day for more than forty years: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Painful swallowing with oropharyngeal dysphagia from the tonsillar tumor: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Unintended weight loss from painful swallowing, about 2 kg before presentation and 9% of body weight by the end of treatment: active, confirmed [S]</item></list><paragraph>Coordinated follow-up with the primary clinician is appropriate. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Order a contrast-enhanced CT of the neck before the specialist visit, and PET/CT for staging once biopsy confirms carcinoma. Guideline: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Tobacco cessation: advise stopping cigars, set a quit date, behavioral counseling at every visit, and varenicline. Guideline: Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021) [S]</item><item>Nutrition: dietitian assessment before treatment, a soft calorie-dense diet with oral supplements, and a weight at every visit; the head and neck team decides on a feeding tube if weight loss nears 10%. Guideline: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Dental evaluation and fluoride care before radiation to the neck. Guideline: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Symptom control with liquid acetaminophen and topical lidocaine, pain scored at each visit, and escalation by the oncology team during treatment. Guideline: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Check CBC, basic metabolic panel, and albumin before and after treatment; baseline TSH before neck radiation, repeated every six to twelve months afterward. Guideline: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression and hypothyroidism monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Screen for depression with the PHQ-2 at each primary care visit after the diagnosis. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression and hypothyroidism monographs (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
